    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Mussaman Curry Sauce\nIngredients\nSalt\nSpice\nChilli\nSugar\nGarlic\nShallot\nGalangal\nFish Sauce\nPeppercorns\nShrimp Paste\nCoconut Milk\nLemon Grass\nSoya Bean Oil\nTamarind Juice\nBenefit for Health\nCoconut Milk : Nourish Body, Tendon and Bone.\nTamarind Juice : Use for Phlegm, Constipation, Cough.\nTG 991 Y - MAR/JUN/SEP/DEC\n1007.086.128",
      "Bangkok - Munich\nPalm Heart Salad, Balsamic Vinaigrette Dressing\nRoast Chicken with Chinese Red Sauce, Steamed Thai Rice\nor\nBroiled Fillet of Pork with Mushroom Cream Sauce, Vegetables\nRoll, Butter\nRed Currant Cheesecake with Vanilla Sauce\nAMAZING THAI FOOD\nTom Kha Gai\n(Chicken Coconut Soup)\nINGREDIENTS\nCoconut milk\nGalangal (a root similar to ginger root)\nBemongrass\nFresh kaffir lime leaves, torn in half\nSliced boneless chicken breast\nFish sauce\nGranulated sugar\nFresh lime juice\nFresh coriander leaves\nThai chili pepper, crushed\n500\n250\n125\n1/4\nml\nstalks\nstalks\nleaves\ngrams\ntБsp.\nIbsp.\nml\ncup\neach\nFresh Fruit Salad and Yoghurt\nBoiled Egg Florentine\nGrilled Chicken, Chicken Sausage and Vegetables\nCrepes filled with Creamed Asparagus, Vegetables\nRoll, Croissant, Butter, Jam\n- Cut the lower part of the lemongrass stalks into 1 inch\npieces then crush to release the oil and aroma.\n- Bring 250 ml of coconut milk to the boil. Add galangal\nlemongrass and kaffir lime leaves.\n- Add chicken, fish sauce and sugar. Cook until chicken is\ntender.\n- Add the rest of the coconut milk and bring back to the boil.\n- Put lime juice into a serving bowl and pour the soup over it.\nGarnish with coriander leaves and crushed fresh chilies.\n** For passengers who prefer a light alternative, we suggest a plate of cheese and cold meat.\nPlease accept our apology if your preference is not available.\nTG 924 Y - MAR/SEP\n2006.034,14"
    ],
